<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Neville's Cross</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1346</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-war-of-scottish-independence">Second War of Scottish Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Neville's Cross was fought on 17 October 1346 near Durham, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-ii-of-scotland">David II of Scotland</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in support of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> after the English victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-crecy">Crécy</a>. An English army raised in the northern counties defeated the Scots, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> II was captured and held in England for eleven years until he was ransomed by the Treaty of Berwick in 1357.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-nevilles-cross.jpg" alt="Battle of Neville's Cross" width="320" height="287" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Froissart · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BNMsFr2643FroissartFol97vBatNevilleCross.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
